## To release a new version, edit the version in the two lines below and nothing else.
## |cRRGGBB...|r in Title and Author colours them in the in-game add-on list; the version
## is read back through that markup, so it can sit inside or outside the colour.
## The settings panel takes its version from ## Title; the name itself is fixed in Main.lua.
## Title: |cFF69B4PB’s MiniMap|r 2.3.4
## Author: |cFF69B4PinkBanther|r
## Description: A lightweight minimap for console. Keeps the game's own world map parked on the HUD at a size and position you choose, and hands it straight back when you open the full map. Inspired by Votan's Minimap by votan, with thanks -- written for console so it stays inside the add-on memory limit.
## Version: 2.3.4
## APIVersion: 101050 101051
## DependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings>=20106
## SavedVariables: PBsMiniMap_Data

## Credit: Inspired by "Votan's Minimap" by votan (https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info1399-VotansMinimap.html).
## The idea of using the game's own world map as the minimap comes from that add-on. This one is written for console; a few small pieces still trace back to it.

